`Debug.Assert(New_arrList_LastIndexOf_x == Old_arrListLastIndexOf_x || New_arrListLastIndexOf_x == Old_index);`

This Debug.Assert statement does the same assertion check, but for the LastIndexOf function. Because LastIndexOf returns the last occurrence of the added element (or the given index if an occurrence does not exist), we need to validate if the new or the old index returned by this method is the correct one.

`Debug.Assert(New_arrListContainsX == true);` and `Debug.Assert(New_arrListContainsX == Old_arrListContainsX);`

These statements ensure that the Contains method correctly indicates whether or not the added element is in the ArrayList, and if Contains previously said the element was in the ArrayList.
  
